          "solution": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef mrmr_mid_select(rel_scores, red_matrix, k: int) -> tuple[list[int], list[float]]:\n    rel = np.asarray(rel_scores, dtype=float)\n    red = np.asarray(red_matrix, dtype=float)\n    remaining = list(range(len(rel)))\n    selected, step_scores = [], []\n    for step in range(k):\n        if step == 0:\n            best = max(remaining, key=lambda j: (rel[j], -j))\n            score = float(rel[best])\n        else:\n            def mid_val(j: int) -> float:\n                return float(rel[j] - np.mean([red[j, s] for s in selected]))\n            best = max(remaining, key=lambda j: (mid_val(j), -j))\n            score = mid_val(best)\n        selected.append(int(best))\n        step_scores.append(round(score, 4))\n        remaining.remove(best)\n    return (selected, step_scores)\n```"
